{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RP-05 D5.1 approved during rebar-brainstorm (2026-08-18): normalize canonical help for every visible top-level command now. Each visible route will have package-data-backed canonical help, and both `rebar <command> --help`/`-h` and `rebar help <command>` will resolve that help before handler loading, optional-capability probing, store mounting, or command execution. This is an intentional behavior change for the 21 intercept-only advanced verbs: `help <command>` becomes successful instead of unknown, and unsafe/inconsistent handler-owned help such as `enrich --help` becomes side-effect-free. Byte authority remains reviewed package data; the registry points to it rather than generating/reflowing it. Hidden compatibility-alias visibility/help behavior remains to be resolved separately. Recovery authority: irascible-clueless-basenji; research note: `.joe-janitor/rp05-cli-registry-research.md`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787068162102295001,"uuid":"acfed787-0b6e-4290-9300-cd3c695cd4c4"}